-- Plan 63 criterion 6: the resolver's boundary, asserted rather than
-- described.
--
-- An **inherent** `instance` has no class, so there is nothing for an elided
-- signature to be taken from. That is a property of the construct and not a
-- limit of the lookup — widening the resolver would not help, because no
-- class is named.
--
-- The other two ways to reach this diagnostic are a class this file does not
-- declare, and a class declared *after* the instance. The message names what
-- it looked for so a reader can tell which of the three they hit.

data Counter = Counter { value : u32 }

instance Counter
  current self = self.value
